WEBVTT

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.250
My little sister, Umaru, is renowned for her beauty.

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:07.700
Umaruu                                    uuuuuuuun

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.160
Yeah, that's enough of that. 

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:47.950
Episode 1: The Himouto Returns

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.040
You're staying there?

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.620
Wait, today's Saturday, right?

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.290
Yeah. I'll be back tomorrow night. 

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:54.000
But it's your day off!

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.660
This is why you're a corporate slave

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.660
to a wicked company that steals your soul. 

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:59.870
Our deadline's right around the corner. 

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.500
Also, I'll get some time off in exchange. 

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.870
Summer vacation's over, so even though

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.870
I won't be around, you better not stay up too late.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.410
Sure. 

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.500
That Evening

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.120
Big Brother...

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.540
is totally gone!

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.410
I'm free, FREE I say!

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:43.330
My night is just getting started!

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.080
Big Brother always goes

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.080
to sleep before midnight, so...

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.040
Go to bed already, or I won't

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.040
be able to wake up tomorrow!

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.790
But this is the time to burn through all my games!

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.450
I just never seem to have enough time!

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:57.830
BATTLE STATS

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.950
BATTLE STATS

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.950
FLAWLESS VICTORY!!

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.040
BATTLE STATS

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.040
FLAWLESS VICTORY!!

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.040
NEXT

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.290
You've encountered a new friend!

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.660
JUKI

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.580
This is a bulldozer. It will protect you. 

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:07.620
Woo-hoo! That's super rare!

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.410
Oh, no. I'm going to wake up Big Brother!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:18.410
He always gets mad, so I just acted out of reflex.  

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.910
Do you know what time it is?!

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.250
GROWWWWL

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.500
Oh, yeah! Big Brother said...

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.410
I made you some breakfast.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.000
It's stir-fried bell peppers...

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.500
Jeez...

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.040
Hey, dammit!

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.410
Now THIS is good food!

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.830
Stop eating cup noodles so late at night!

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.700
Don't drink all the soup!

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.950
POTATO

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.950
CHIPS

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.290
Late-night potato chips and cola sure hit the spot!

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.040
It's late, so keep your voice down!

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.750
Quit eating those potato chips!

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:10.540
Stop chugging it!

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:15.910
But now, no one can get mad at me. 

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.330
I have everything in the palm of my hand!

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.830
Today, Umaru shall be held down by NO ONE!

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.950
This is a world where nights are long and glorious!

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.910
But, I thought it was 1:00 AM!

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.450
Sure enough, time flies at this hour.   

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.200
Time to check what late-night anime are on!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.830
It's morning. Get up, Umaru!

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.290
Hng... what? It's morning already?

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.500
Huh?

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:59.870
I stayed up late, so I slept in more than usual!

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.580
What the heck?!

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:05.200
I've burned through 16 hours!

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.080
What are you doing outside?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:25.290
Huh? I thought if I went out, I could

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:25.290
get back some of what I'd burned through.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.370
"Burned through"?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.500
It's dangerous to be out at night.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.500
Hurry up and get back inside!

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.830
I'm not sure what's going on, but... I'm home. 

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.040
Yup. Welcome back!

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.750
Sunday

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.000
Well, let's go, Umaru!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.290
What are you talking about, Big Brother?

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.200
Attendance

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.200
Optional 

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.200
Yoshida Co-op

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.200
Request for Help with Property Weeding

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:56.200
It's "attendance optional," right? No one's gonna go!

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:01.080
Plus, it's still September! It'll be hot! You go by yourself. 

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.790
Oh, really...?

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.160
Well, the landlord might find that a little strange. 

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.160
Like, "Umaru is such a nice girl,

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.160
so I thought for sure she'd come."

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:16.910
My, I'm glad to see some youngsters showing up.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:20.660
As you can see, my back is giving me some problems...

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.830
Please, just rest a while. 

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:32.160
Okay, Big Brother... let's go home. 

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.200
Wait up!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.120
Huh?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.450
The heck? There aren't even that many of them. 

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.290
Hya! Hya!

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.250
Hya!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.290
Ebina?

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:50.870
Ah! T-Taihei and Umaru! Good morning. 

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.370
So you're here too, huh?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:56.080
I-I only just got started. 

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.450
Great job, Ebina. You've already pulled all those? 

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:04.120
Ah! Well, back home in Akita,

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:04.120
reckon I... I mean, I'm used to this! 

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.700
You're a world apart from Umaru... 

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:15.370
Anyway, I'm glad you're both here.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:15.370
Honestly, I was a little lonely on my own. 

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.950
Y-yeah. I bet. 

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.830
Looks like it's hard for her to go running off now. 

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.290
Say, why don't we do this together?

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.910
O-okay!

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.830
Um... so, should I cut these with a sickle? 

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.910
Ah! I think it'd be best to pull them by hand.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.120
You have to pull them by the roots

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:33.120
or else they'll grow back. 

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.200
Hya!

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.620
Okay, well, here goes...

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.950
The heck? This is... kind of fun!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:53.000
Giant weed spotted dead ahead!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:53.000
That must be the middle boss!

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.540
THE TYPE

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.540
THAT GETS

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.540
FIRED UP

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:55.540
EASILY

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.450
One, two...

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.620
Hey, are you okay?

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.290
Big Brother! I quit! I'm going home!

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.950
You can if you want.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.950
Big Brother! I quit! I'm going home!

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:15.660
Sorry for dragging out here in this heat. 

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.410
You're not hurt, are you?

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:21.200
Hya! Hya! 

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.910
I can do this a little longer. 

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.370
Ebina, let me help you. 

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.950
O-okay!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.080
We finished up pretty fast, huh? 

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:44.500
Yes! It feels like we've really done something here.  

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.330
Ebina, your face is all red.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.330
Are you having a heatstroke? 

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.330
N-no, I'm not!

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.660
Are you really okay?

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.450
I-I super really am!

00:08:58.910 --> 00:08:59.750
Oh?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:04.450
Well, how about we all treat ourselves

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:04.450
by getting something cold to eat?

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.500
Ooh! Great idea, Big Brother!

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.200
O-okay. Thank you very much. 

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.370
A soccer match?

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.200
My school shall be holding it this month. 

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.080
Huh?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:20.080
I totally forgot...

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.790
This is why I must practice! 

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:31.870
SHBWAA               AAAAA!

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.620
What was that move just now?!

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.700
Potato Catch!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.750
Stop kicking your food!

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:41.500
It's just something I do at home sometimes,

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:41.500
the Potato Catch...

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:46.750
You're quite good at ball games, yes? Please, teach me!

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:52.950
Sylphyn and I are always battling each other, 

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:52.950
but the soccer match will be class vs. class.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.750
This might make it easier to talk to her at school. 

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.910
You think you can keep up with my training regimen?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.660
Note: Osu! Is commonly used in martial arts circles as a way of not only

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.660
agreeing, but to also show determination.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.660
OSU! Yes, Ma'am!

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:04.910
TSF!

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:10.790
Don't watch the ball. Instead,

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:10.790
see the trajectory of where the ball is GOING.  

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.370
Understood!

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.870
Mentality is a big part of sports.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.700
You have to visualize you've already won. 

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.660
When you take your shot,

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:20.660
the ball should spin like a bullet...

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.120
like you're blasting it with a laser!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.750
BEST FRIENDS

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.580
The ball is your best friend... 

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.790
The ball is your lover!

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.330
Save your stamina for when you'll need it.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:39.540
Take some breaks during the game. Rest is important. 

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.410
But if I rest, I will have points detracted. 

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:49.250
Soccer is a team sport.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:49.250
Just take your break and trust in the others!

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.290
I... 

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:57.830
I wanted to be at the same school,

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:57.830
in the same class as you, UMR. 

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:06.200
Th-the people in your class are good at soccer too.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:06.200
Now take what I've taught you and go WIN!

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.950
Yes! Indeed!

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:13.250
SOCCER MATCH

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.620
So, these are the uniforms we'll all be wearing...

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:18.500
Kirie!

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:22.870
I will protect Umaru... I will protect Umaru...

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:22.870
I WILL protect Umaru!

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:27.040
I'm not feeling very confident. 

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.000
Ebina!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.660
You'll be fine. 

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:34.950
I wish I was on the same team as you.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.500
Huh? Speaking of...

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:39.580
Our uniforms are different. 

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.580
ARAYADA

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.250
All right, let's get this match underway!

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.540
Everyone, take your places. 

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.870
Wait, who are these people?

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.870
Most of them aren't even in our class!

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.500
Uh, well...

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.330
They split up our classes

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.330
when they were making the teams.  

00:11:55.830 --> 00:12:00.250
The students were getting too fired up about it

00:11:55.830 --> 00:12:00.250
being class vs. class, so they scrapped the idea.  

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:05.370
They tried to balance out the teams, and made the

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:05.370
person with the best grades in PE the leader. 

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.040
The person with the best grades is the leader?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.750
Wait, don't tell me...!

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:13.250
Huh? Your leader hasn't gotten here yet? 

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:14.540
Here I am!

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.000
Shapaaaaaaan!

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:23.620
SHAPAAAAAAAAN!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.950
She's standing on some balls

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.950
and sliding around on them?!

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.540
It's like she's water skiing!

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:30.620
Shbwaaa!

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.250
Shbwaaa                           aaaaaaan!

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:35.200
I have trained quite extensively!

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:35.200
It is through soccer that I shall defeat Umaru!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.410
Why is this happening?

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:42.040
Okay, it looks like it's almost time for kickoff. 

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:46.500
This match will be between Arayada High's Team T...

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.370
and their opponent, Team U!

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.290
And there's the whistle!

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:56.120
Whoa! Sylphyn has shot forward!

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:59.000
See the trajectory of where the ball is GOING.  

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:01.620
Shbwaaaaa!

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:01.660
Shbwaaa!

00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.080
Indeed! 

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.160
Now THAT'S fast! 

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:03.830
SHBWAAAAA!

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:06.160
SHBWAAA!

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.700
Her form is all over the place,

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.700
but her power is remarkable!

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:07.830
SHBWAAA!

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:09.750
The time is now:

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:14.330
Canzone Sylphyn Bullet Shoot!

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:17.290
Laser Beam!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.620
It's so fast! Is this a done deal?!

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.250
Huh?

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.250
Kirie?!

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:25.160
This is... a misdirection!

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:29.620
Kirie has changed the ball's trajectory

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:29.620
and sent it straight to Umaru.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:30.700
That was awesome!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:32.750
Okay, we're on the offensive!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.450
I wanted to fight alongside Sylphyn,

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.040
but still... I'm going to give this all I've got!

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:42.700
The ball...

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.200
I can see its trajectory!

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:48.540
Umaru and Sylphyn are locked in a heated battle! 

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:49.790
SPACE STREAM GRAND CROSS

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:49.790
Umaru and Sylphyn are locked in a heated battle!

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:54.620
SPACE STREAM GRAND CROSS

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:54.620
I'm not sure what the caption at the bottom there

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:54.620
means, but is that a universe I see forming?!

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.700
Oh, no! I've had to deal with

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.700
so many surprises that now I feel weak!

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:00.000
Indeed!

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:08.540
GOAL!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.450
The first point of the game goes to Team T!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:16.830
Sylphyn pulled it off all on her own, and despite

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:16.830
how far she ran, she's not breathing heavy at all!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.370
I... I pushed myself a bit too far. 

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:28.790
That play just now took a lot out of me.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:28.790
Regardless, I must score another point!

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:32.660
S-Sylphyn! Wait! 

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:52.870
Team U has rallied around Umaru

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:52.870
and is holding their own against Team T!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:57.580
Meanwhile, Sylphyn has turned

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:57.580
Team T into a one-man show!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.660
Kirie! Just do it!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:07.540
U-Umaru is cheering me on! 

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:13.200
Take... Take THAT!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:18.160
This shot has given the ball a strange gyration!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:18.160
But will it hit net?!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:27.080
Later, the judge who witnessed this mysterious

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:27.080
incident explained it as follows:

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.750
Yeah, I'd never seen anything like it. 

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.000
Normally, a ball strikes

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.000
and then rebounds like this, right?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.580
But in this case... 

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:43.000
The ball hit a sort of soft obstruction,

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:43.000
resulting in a motion nothing short of miraculous. 

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:48.500
No one could have predicted

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:48.500
what the ball would do next! Put simply...

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:56.000
It scored a picture-perfect goal against Team T.  

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:59.330
It's an OWN GOAL! That's as good as any!

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.500
It's not "good" at all!

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.910
I shan't allow you to score!

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:17.120
What turn of events is this?

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:17.120
Team U is starting to pick up the pace!

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.080
How can the other team keep this up?

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.200
D-don't tell me...!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.540
Yes, they're in the zone!

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:31.950
Team U has reached that ultimate

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:31.950
state of focus known as "the zone"!

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:36.500
(For more about this "zone," please see

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:36.500
whichever sports manga is applicable.) 

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:40.910
But how? How can there be such

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:40.910
a difference between our teams?

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.500
At this rate, defeat is certain!

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:48.910
I practiced so hard, and even

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:48.910
received instruction from... UMR!

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:51.000
Soccer is a team sport. 

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:57.290
Tanabe! Take a wide right!

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.580
Huh? O-okay.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:03.660
Daimoji! Cover Sakura a bit so she can rest.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.700
U-understood. 

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.000
Ebina!

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.040
I'm counting on you!

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:11.540
O-okay. 

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:20.870
What's going on?

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.160
Suddenly, they're moving a lot more coordinated!

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:25.000
U-Umaru?

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:28.330
This fight is ON!

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:29.830
TSF!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.160
Team T

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.160
Team U

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.790
And time is up!

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:42.120
Team U came from behind for the win!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:47.870
Sylphyn...

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.580
You were great, Sylphyn!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.000
How did you fire off that "Bullet Shot"?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:56.120
But, I mean, we lost...

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.580
You scored two points against

00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:59.580
Umaru's team, and that's amazing!

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:01.950
Plus, your coaching in the second half was fantastic!

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.450
You even remembered all our names, right?

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:07.660
Well... yes...

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.330
Please teach us soccer sometime!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:12.700
Yes, indeed!

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:17.830
And so, the soccer match came to a close... 

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.620
We'll be having a volleyball tournament soon.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.410
I certainly hope we can train together again!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.950
...and the next ball match was already

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.950
right around the corner. 

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:34.660
Hey! Let's all walk home together!

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.330
Y-you're that girl from the class next door, uh...

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:39.700
I'm Haruka! C'mon, let's go!

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:42.250
Hey! I don't even know you,

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:42.250
so stop talking like you're my friend!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:43.910
C'mon, don't sweat the details!

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:46.330
Jeez... well, fine. 

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:52.080
I swear... Haruka is always making friends

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:52.080
with that dazzling smile of hers. 

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.370
HA              RU              KA

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.950
Making friends with a simple greeting

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.950
like that sure would make things easier, huh?

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:02.370
But, I mean, it is what it is, right?

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:05.450
Even asking someone to hang out

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:05.450
is way too much pressure!

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:07.410
What if you ask and they say no?

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:10.290
You'll be heartbroken, and you won't even have a friend!

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:12.450
Say, let's walk home together! 

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.290
You're being WAY too dramatic!

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.830
If that sort of thing holds you back,

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:19.830
you'll just regret it later. 

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:22.580
Did you have lots of friends?

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:38.870
Kirie, you and Umaru made some

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:38.870
awesome combo plays at the soccer match!

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.660
N-no, I wouldn't say that...

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:45.410
Sylphyn, do you understand this question?

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:46.750
Yes, indeed!

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:53.870
It seems like people are talking to Kirie and Sylphyn

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:53.870
a lot more after the soccer match...

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:57.290
Maybe I should try talking to people too. 

00:19:58.000 --> 00:19:59.040
Huh?!

00:19:59.410 --> 00:20:01.870
I-I'm embarrassed for some reason. 

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.250
Also... what would I do if they're not interested?

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
S

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
H

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
B

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
W

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
A

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
A

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:07.500
A

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:13.410
Oh. I've always been the one

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:13.410
that other people talk to first... 

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:19.200
I wonder if Kirie has club activities...

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:21.450
She wasn't in her class, so I think so. 

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:27.450
Maybe if I joined a club,

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:27.450
I could get good at sports like you.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:30.250
Are you thinking about the soccer match?

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:33.700
Yes. I made so many mistakes...

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:37.370
Still, Sylphyn was kind enough to pass the ball to me. 

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:39.410
It was a lot of fun!

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:47.500
I thought about talking to Sylphyn after that,

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:47.500
but she said she had to talk to a friend and just left.  

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:52.290
Ebina, you've asked Kirie

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:52.290
to have lunch with you before, right?

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.200
Weren't you afraid she'd say "No"?

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:59.620
Yes. I was embarrassed and a little unsure...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.500
But I felt I'd regret it if I didn't try!

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.450
Umaru?

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:10.200
I... I'm going to look for Sylphyn, and-

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.700
Um! Our tests are coming up, so...!

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:19.620
Ah! Um, they're cleaning the pool today,

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:19.620
so club activities are...!

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:24.750
Say, how about the four of us walk home together?

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.700
Y-you certainly are asking a lot.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.910
B-but, fine, I have no objections!

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:34.540
Uh... Yes, YES!

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:40.870
Ah, it's Umaru!

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:43.750
Huh. So those four are friends?

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:45.290
And here we go! Indeed!

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:47.080
Please calm yourself, Sylphyn.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.080
So, where should we go?

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.660
What do you say we get some crepes? 

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:50.620
Sounds great!

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:40.830
Next Episode

00:23:25.870 --> 00:23:40.830
